the Japanese population, 27,572 MS patients and 1,436,801 controls in the European population, 819 MS patients and 155,904 controls in the African population, and 29,374 MS patients and 1,843,563 controls in the cross-population (293 MS patients and 45,569 controls in the US population was included) and Single-cell RNA-seq data from 20 MS patients\",{\"_415\":1255},\"401 Moyamoya diseasepatients and 47,255 controls\",{\"_415\":1257},\"Myasthenia gravis cases: 1,434 (Japan MG Registry), Control participants: 42,913 (BioBank Japan)\",{\"_415\":1259},\"Japanese male asthma patients: 3 cases, Japanese male COVID-19 patients: 4 cases\",{\"_415\":1261},\"161,026 Japanese males (BBJ: 120,522, JCTF: 3,161, TMM: 26,544, COVC: 888, HERPACC: 6,636, JPHC: 3,275)\",{\"_415\":1263},\"Populations: Biobank Japan (n = 166,757) and UK biobank (n = 273,453), Phenotypes: 374\",{\"_415\":1265},\"Psoriasis cases: 1,415, Control participants: 3,968\",{\"_415\":1267},\"Single-cell RNA-sequencing for PBMC from 15 COVID-19 patients and 72 healthy controls of Japanese\",{\"_415\":1269},\"Plasma proteomics data from 83 COVID-19 patients and 144 healthy controls of Japanese\",{\"_415\":1271},\"Single-cell eQTL summary statistics of 40 immune cell types for Japanese population (COVID-19: n = 88, Healthy controls: n = 146)\",{\"_415\":1273},\"Neuromyelitis optica spectrum disorders (NMOSD) cases: 240, Control participants: 50,578\",{\"_415\":1275},\"HPV-associated oropharyngeal cancer cases: 32, Non-HPV-associated oropharyngeal cancer cases: 17, Healthy controls: 2\",{\"_415\":1277},\"The first cohort of BioBank Japan (n = 171,287)\",{\"_415\":1279},\"Autoimmune diseases cases: 2,238, Healthy controls: 2,919\",{\"_415\":1281},\"Recurrent pregnancy loss cases: 1,728, Control participants: 24,315\",{\"_415\":1283},\"The weights of variants existing in the target cohorts, Tohoku Medical Megabank and the second cohort of BBJ, calculated from GWAS results on 27,642 type 2 diabetes cases and 70,242 controls from BioBank Japan and UK Biobank\",{\"_415\":1285},\"524 Japanese individuals for gut microbiome-host genome association analysis, 362 Japanese individuals for plasma metabolite-host genome association analysis\",{\"_415\":1287},\"Hunner-type interstitial cystitis cases: 144, Control participants: 41,516\",{\"_415\":1289},\"BioBank Japan (n=180,215), UK Biobank (n=377,441), and large-scale meta-analysis including the summary statistics of other cohorts [FinnGen, Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC), and Prostate Cancer Association Group to Investigate Cancer Associated Alterations in the Genome (PRACTICAL)] for breast and prostate cancer (n=648,746 and 482,080), Phenotypes: 15\",{\"_415\":1291},\"Metagenomic data of gut microbiome in the Japanese population (88 + 5 individuals) and healthy individuals (n = 73)\",{\"_415\":1293},\"Microbial genome: Metagenome-Assembled Genome (MAG), Viral genome, CRISPR spacers\",{\"_415\":1295},\"Peripheral blood mononuclear cell (PBMC) from Japanese population (COVID-19: n = 30 + 43, Healthy controls: n = 31 + 44)\",{\"_415\":1297},\"Populations: Biobank Japan (n = 161,801) and UK biobank (n = 377,583), Phenotypes: 9\",{\"_415\":1299},\"Intracranial germ cell tumors cases: 133, Control participants: 762\",{\"_415\":1301},\"Metagenomic data of gut microbiome in Inflammatory Bowel Disease (35 Ulcerative Colitis and 39 Crohn's disease) and 40 Healthy controls\",{\"_415\":1303},\"141 Japanese individuals\",{\"_415\":1305},\"Populations: Biobank Japan (n = 179,000), UK biobank (n = 361,000), and FinnGen (n = 136,000), Phenotypes: 220\",{\"_415\":1307},\"Autoimmune pulmonary alveolar proteinosis cases: 198, Control participants: 395\",{\"_415\":1309},\"Metagenomic data of gut microbiome in the Japanese population (95 + 103 + 227 + 30 + 136 individuals)\",[1311],[1312],{\"_415\":1313},\"Metagenome shotgun sequencing, genome-wide association study (GWAS), small RNA-seq and eQTL analyses, whole genome sequencing (WGS), single-cell RNA sequencing, proteomics\",[1315],[1316],{\"_415\":32},[1318,1319],[1322],[1320],{\"_415\":1321},\"- RNAs extracted from PBMCs of 20 MS patients were subjected to single-cell RNA-seq analysis. Integrated data are provided (h5ad file).\",{\"_415\":1323},\"DNAs extracted from peripheral blood cells of multiple sclerosis (MS) patients and conrols (688 MS patients and 205,199 controls in the Japanese population, 27,572 MS patients and 1,436,801 controls in the European population, 819 MS patients and 155,904 controls in the African population, and 29,374 MS patients and 1,843,563 controls in the cross-population (293 MS patients and 45,569 controls in the US population was included).) were genotyped and performed genome-wide association study. A tsv file is provided.\",\"alerts\",[1330,1331,1332],\"account\",\"site\",{\"_13\":14,\"_1329\":272},\"noindex\",{\"_1333\":1336,\"_271\":272},{\"_1333\":1335,\"_271\":272},{\"_1333\":1334,\"_271\":272},\"html\",\"\u003cp\u003eFollowing a change to our organizational structure effective April 1, 2026, this division has been renamed from the \\\"Database Center for Life Science, Joint Support-Center for Data Science Research\\\" to the \\\"Database Division for Life Science (DBCLS), BioData Science Initiative (BSI), National Institute of Genetics (NIG)\\\". Where the former name still appears in the guidelines, please read it as the new name.\u003c/p\u003e\",\"\u003cp\u003eWe are currently receiving a large number of applications for data submission, and the review process is taking longer than usual.We sincerely apologize for the delay and kindly ask for your understanding. When submitting an application, we would greatly appreciate it if you could allow sufficient time for the processing.\u003c/p\u003e\",\"\u003cp\u003eDue to system maintenance, the application system, application review by the Data Access Committee will be unavailable during the following period.\u003cbr\u003e\\nSchedule: October 5th (Mon), 2026, 9:00 - October 7th (Wed), 2026, 15:00 (JST)\u003cbr\u003e\\nWe apologize for any inconvenience this may cause and appreciate your understanding.\u003c/p\u003e\"]\n");</script><!--$--><script>window.__reactRouterContext.streamController.close();</script><!--/$--><!--/$--></body></html>